+On a direct 200 Gb/s DGX Spark link, `ib` avoids the socket staging path.
+The launcher also leaves P2P/SHM enabled for this one-GPU-per-node topology.
+The old TCP compatibility profile (`IB`, `P2P`, and `SHM` disabled) required
+about 43 ms of FlashSAC gradient synchronization per iteration; the validated
+RoCE profile requires a median 11.4 ms. Use the default `tcp` transport when
+the RDMA device is not active on both hosts.
+
